<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maha Bandula</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1782">1782</a>–<a href="/years/1825">1825</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maha Bandula was a Burmese general of the Konbaung dynasty who led campaigns in Manipur and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> and on the frontier of British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-burmese-war">First Anglo-Burmese War</a> he commanded the Burmese armies against the British, was defeated near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Yangon</a> in December 1824, and was killed at Danubyu on 1 April 1825. He is honoured in Myanmar as a national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maha-bandula.jpg" alt="Maha Bandula" width="320" height="657" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kantabon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statute_of_Maha_Bandula.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
